// `bool` — the two-constructor tier-0 declaration and nothing else yet.
//
// Moved out of `nat` (2026-08-05), where it lived because `leb` needed it.
// The module earns more the day it has a second thing to say: `not`/`and`
// and their laws, or a general reflection kit (`nat`'s decided order —
// `Le(n, m)` as `leb(n)(m) = True` — is the pattern any decidable
// proposition over any type repeats, and its Bool half belongs here).

inductive Bool { False, True }
